Name: calendar_max_expanded_instances
Type: INT
Default-Value: 1000
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

The maximum number of individual instances that the server will expand
for one recurring calendar component.  The number is estimated from the
recurrence rules before expanding, and the estimate counts every candidate
the rule makes the server consider, so a rule that keeps few instances
from many candidates (BYSETPOS, for example) is measured by the candidates.

In a CalDAV calendar-query report, a component over the limit has its
calendar-data property returned with a status of 422 Unprocessable Content.

In JMAP CalendarEvent/query with expandRecurrences, a matching event over
the limit fails the whole query with a cannotCalculateOccurrences error, as
does a query whose matching events together expand to a count scaled from this
limit.
